@RULEL:TRANSPOSED_SOURCE:1.0
~METADATA{original=".cursorrules" ext=""}
.source{content="# LIN Language Rules for AI Agents (Cursor, OpenCode, Antigravity, Cline)\nYou are an expert developer in LIN (Língua IA Nativa — @LIN:L1c:0.2).\n\n## Core Syntax Rules:\n1. Always start code with `@LIN:L1c:0.2`\n2. Functions: `!fn_name(param1, param2) { ... }`\n3. Return: `^expression;`\n4. Conditions: `?(condition) { ... }` or `if (condition) { ... }`\n5. Loops: `while (cond) { ... }` or `for (...) { ... }`\n6. Exports: `=ex{fn1, fn2}`\n\n## Toolchain Commands:\n- Validate syntax: `lin check <file.lin>`\n- Compile to native binary ELF: `lin compile <file.lin> -o <binary>`\n- Execute directly: `lin run <file.lin> [function] [args...]`\n- Convert foreign code to LIN: `lin to-lin <file> -o <file.lin>`\n"}
